# Vauxhall Viva HA two-door saloon, 1963-1966.
#
# Vauxhall's first small car after the war: 3,937 mm long, 1,524 mm wide,
# 1,346 mm high, 2,324 mm wheelbase; 1,057 cc overhead-valve four, four-speed
# gearbox, front disc brakes optional. Replaced by the HB in 1966.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Viva
#
# Colours: White, Red, Blue and Green are documented Vauxhall colours of the
# period.
#
# Weight: 100 in total (white 30, red 25, blue 25, green 20).
#
# Speed 125 km/h; comfort 55/413 (line). Classes 1,2.
# Dates: 1963-1966 with a road tail to about 1980.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-viva-ha.blend. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-viva-ha/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
